<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hiroshima Prefecture</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hiroshima">Hiroshima</a> Prefecture is a prefecture in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chugoku-region">Chūgoku region</a> of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honshu">Honshu</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, on the Inland Sea, with its capital at Hiroshima. It was formed in 1871 from the Hiroshima domain of the Asano and covers the old provinces of Aki and Bingo. It contains the shrine of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/itsukushima">Itsukushima</a> and the naval port of Kure.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hiroshima-prefecture.jpg" alt="Hiroshima Prefecture" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DXR · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peace_Memorial_Park_and_Cenotaph,_Hiroshima,_South_view_20190417_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
